  {
   "id": "c-constant-pressure",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The canonical ensemble holds the number of particles, the volume and the temperature constant, as Section 17.2 says; the pressure is not fixed."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-molecular-q",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "For a fraction of molecules, the sum in the denominator runs over the states of one molecule: it is the molecular partition function $q$ of Section 17.2. The same equation holds with $Q$ when $E_i$ are the energies of the states of the whole system, which is how the rest of this section uses it."
  }
 ],
